208 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (Violence is a public health issue driven by a complex interplay of environmental, systemic, and social stressors. Gun violence, particularly homicides, is a pressing concern in New Orleans. The rate of firearm homicides is measured per 100,000 people, and it is particularly alarming that Black residents are disproportionately affected. In New Orleans, the homicide rate for Black residents is 58.9, which is notably higher than the rate of 37.6 in comparable cities. To address this crisis, the New Orleans Health Department's Office of Violence Prevention is taking proactive steps, including offering firearm safe storage, deploying peace ambassadors, employing violence interrupters, and providing supportive services for both children and adults impacted by gun violence. These efforts aim to reduce violence and support those most affected by it.)
/E (Violence is a public health issue driven by a complex interplay of environmental, systemic, and social stressors. Gun violence, particularly homicides, is a pressing concern in New Orleans. The rate of firearm homicides is measured per 100,000 people, and it is particularly alarming that Black residents are disproportionately affected. In New Orleans, the homicide rate for Black residents is 58.9, which is notably higher than the rate of 37.6 in comparable cities. To address this crisis, the New Orleans Health Department's Office of Violence Prevention is taking proactive steps, including offering firearm safe storage, deploying peace ambassadors, employing violence interrupters, and providing supportive services for both children and adults impacted by gun violence. These efforts aim to reduce violence and support those most affected by it.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
