/T (Food Swamps and Food Deserts: A Growing Health Disparity in New Orleans A food swamp refers to an urban area where residents have limited access to grocery stores but are surrounded by non-nutritious options like corner stores and fast-food outlets. In contrast, a food desert is a neighborhood with limited access to affordable, nutritious, and plentiful food. Both conditions contribute to significant health disparities in our communities.)
/E (Food Swamps and Food Deserts: A Growing Health Disparity in New Orleans A food swamp refers to an urban area where residents have limited access to grocery stores but are surrounded by non-nutritious options like corner stores and fast-food outlets. In contrast, a food desert is a neighborhood with limited access to affordable, nutritious, and plentiful food. Both conditions contribute to significant health disparities in our communities.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [12]
>>
