428 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 778 0 R
/ActualText (The Chronic Disease Program promotes health equity for all New Orleanians by bringing together local organizations from across sectors to consider the social factors that lead to chronic illness, developing initiatives that aim to prevent and reduce the prevalence of these illnesses, and by providing programmatic support and management for public health interventions that address high rates of conditions such as diabetes, obesity and food insecurity as well as focusing our efforts on communities most impacted by the social determinants of health. Our team achieves this by working in close partnership with community organizations and by promoting public health policies that secure better health outcomes for all.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
